#: ../../source/components_basic/06-component_button.rst:99
msgid "**Setting Up**: In this part of the code, we first declare the ``sensorPin`` as a constant integer and assign it the pin number we will connect our button to on the Arduino board. The ``setup()`` function sets the mode of the ``sensorPin`` as ``INPUT``, meaning we'll be receiving data in through this pin from the button. The ``Serial.begin()`` function initiates serial communication at a baud rate of 9600."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/06-component_button.rst:110
msgid "**The Loop**: The ``loop()`` function contains the main logic of the program. It continuously reads the button state and prints it to the serial monitor every 50 milliseconds. The ``digitalRead()`` function reads the state of the button, and the ``Serial.println()`` function prints this value to the serial monitor. The ``delay()`` function then pauses the execution for 50 milliseconds before the next reading. The button outputs a low level when pressed, and a high level when released."
msgstr ""

